/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1061 20568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12763dad-dbd5-5f26-bc50-389926344c0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a collection of $n$ objects, there are $n!$ ways to arrange those objects in a sequence.\n\n- For example, suppose we have $n=2$ objects: $A$ and $B.$ Then there are $2!=2 \\cdot 1 = 2$ arrangements:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{A,B}_{1\\text{st way}}, \\quad \\underbrace{B,A}_{2\\text{nd way}}\n$$\n\n- Likewise, suppose we have $n=3$ objects: $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ Then there are $3!=3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 = 6$ arrangements:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{A,B,C}_{1\\text{st way}},\\quad\n\\underbrace{A,C,B}_{2\\text{nd way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{B,A,C}_{3\\text{rd way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{B,C,A}_{4\\text{th way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{C,A,B}_{5\\text{th way}},\\quad \n\\underbrace{C,B,A}_{6\\text{th way}}\n$$\n\nThis pattern extends to any number of objects." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1065 3680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0753e8b5-a022-5644-84fc-f43f1dcf6761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1064 "The mathematical name for an arrangement is a **permutation**. With a permutation, *the order matters*. This means that for the letters $A,B,C,D,E$, the permutation\n\n$$\nA,B,C,D,E\n$$\n\n    is different from\n\n$$\nE,D,C,B,A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1065 3681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "29dee738-c115-51e6-b129-3ddb6d812d68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1067 "Permutations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281762 #edb/ref 1080 "120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281762 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281762 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08737316-aa20-5df6-851c-dce808b637e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281914 #edb/ref 1080 "25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18fd45dc-1ede-51cf-9585-369b367a8961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282820 #edb/ref 1080 "95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282820 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282820 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "82a108e9-b949-5ec3-82d9-001193cc0c6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283290 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283290 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283290 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b939e1e9-b6b5-5e42-8a94-194f830d95e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283739 #edb/ref 1080 "115" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283739 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283739 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ea97fa87-edd6-5cc7-984b-14ae7f4f6d7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186283290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284106 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6814504a-adfe-5300-8bd4-6599a98f28d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1804" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $5$ pictures are to be hung from left to right in a hallway. In how many possible ways can they be hung?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53fbad36-9779-558b-839c-131c419555eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284784 #edb/ref 1074 "There are $n=5$ pictures, so the number of possible arrangements is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5! & =5\\times 4\\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $120$ ways of arranging the $5$ pictures." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
